 BravenSpawner is an independent implementation. It is not affiliated with,
 endorsed by, or derived from the source of any commercial spawner plugin.
+
+## Continuation commands and behavior
+
+`/bspawner sellwand <player> [uses|Nd|inf] [amount]` grants a wand;
+`/bspawner modifier <player> <type> <value> [amount]` grants a cursor-applied modifier.
+`/bspawner boosteritem <player> <normal|personal> <id> [amount]` grants a configured booster.
+Normal effects activate on a spawner; personal XP/cash items work while carried.
+Timed effects currently reset after restart.
+
+Virtual output is aggregated by item identity, so large quantities do not allocate one
+inventory slot for every vanilla stack. Collect or sell stored items before breaking
+a spawner. Remaining XP is returned after optional Mending. Product restrictions can
+lock menus or allow selling while blocking raw withdrawals; the bypass permission is
+`bravenspawner.restrictions.bypass` (operator by default).
+
+Shop prices come from the selected configured provider, with local product/global
+prices as fallback when the provider has no quote. An explicit local zero price
+blocks local selling; a configured external shop can supply its own price. Provider
+stock limits, taxes and special currencies are not processed as shop transactions.
+Only Vault settlement is implemented. WorldGuard is the implemented claim API;
+other land plugins still require qualification or adapters.
+
+Full parity is **not complete**: legacy server versions, the original binary API,
+reference database migration, additional currency/shop/land providers, ItemsAdder
+metadata and remaining visual effects are tracked in the parity report.
